From 30a6c384f4b020280c01ba5a4ba292bbdfab413f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheCryptoDonkey <TheCryptoDonkey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 13:22:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] fix: frame a sideloaded gated app over https on an https
 dashboard

portAuth read the port's auth from the signed catalogue only, so an app
the catalogue does not list was never treated as gate-fronted and kept
the daemon's http:// runtime URL, which an HTTPS dashboard blocks as
mixed content.

Fall back to the daemon-reported lan-port-auth when the catalogue has no
answer. The catalogue stays authoritative where it has one, and ports
that are not gated or open are unchanged.
